```java
import java.util.*;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        List<String> forms = new ArrayList<>();
        
        Map<String, String> data = new HashMap<>();
        data.put("name1", "John");
        data.put("age1", "30");
        forms.add("<form action=\"http://example.com\\\" name=\"form1\">Name:<input type=\"text\" name=\"name1\"><br><br>Age:<input type=\"number\" name=\"age1\"><br><br><button type=\"submit\">Submit</button></form>");
        
        Map<String, String> data2 = new HashMap<>();
        data2.put("name2", "Alice");
        data2.put("age2", "25");
        forms.add("<form action=\"http://example.com\\\" name=\"form2\">Name:<input type=\"text\" name=\"name2\"><br><br>Age:<input type=\"number\" name=\"age2\"><br><br><button type=\"submit\">Submit</button></form>");
        
        Map<String, String> data3 = new HashMap<>();
        data3.put("name3", "Bob");
        data3.put("age3", "35");
        forms.add("<form action=\"http://example.com\\\" name=\"form3\">Name:<input type=\"text\" name=\"name3\"><br><br>Age:<input type=\"number\" name=\"age3\"><br><br><button type=\"submit\">Submit</button></form>");
        
        System.out.println("Form 1: " + forms.get(0));
    }
}

class FormElement {
    public String name;
    public String value;

    public void setName(String name) {
        this.name = name;
    }

    public void setValue(String value) {
        this.value = value;
    }

    @Override
    public String toString() {
        return "Name: " + name + "\n" +
                "Age: " + value + "\n";
    }
}
```

In the above code, we are creating a map where each key-value pair represents a form with its action and form field names. We then iterate over this map to generate three forms with different data.

The `FormElement` class is used to represent individual form fields in Java. The `toString()` method is overridden to provide a string representation of the form element, which can be useful for debugging or logging purposes.

When you run this code, it will print out each form as a separate line, followed by its field names and values.
